Package: CaribTTM
Type: Package
Title: Island-Based Trophic Transfer Model for Data-Limited U.S. Caribbean Fisheries
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matt", "Woodstock", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mandy", "Karnauskas", role = "aut"),
    person("Juan", "Agar", role = "ctb"),
    person("Daniel", "Solis", role = "ctb"),
    person("Ryan", "Vandermeulen", role = "ctb"))
Description: A data-limited, habitat-resolved trophic transfer model (TTM) that
    converts benthic (habitat-specific) and pelagic (satellite or ocean-model)
    net primary production into trophic-level energy pools, partitions that
    energy among Fishery Management Plan (FMP) stock complexes and non-fishery
    functional groups, and projects guild- and group-level multispecies maximum
    sustainable yield (MMSY) through time under oceanographic, habitat,
    disturbance (hurricanes, bleaching, disease) and fishery conditions.
    Uncertainty is propagated by Monte Carlo sampling and optionally conditioned
    on abundance indices with Sampling-Importance-Resampling (SIR). Outputs
    include gear-specific MMSY allocations, choke-group diagnostics, and
    tables formatted for stochastic production frontier (SPF) analyses, as
    described in SEDAR103-DW-20.
